    "environment": [
      "### General",
      "**Primary use of Claude Code**: software development on work and personal repositories (Java/Spring, .NET, TypeScript, Docker, AWS)",
      "**Repository visibility**: treat every work repository as private; public paste or gist services are outside the trust boundary",
      "**Trusted source control**: each repository's own origin remote only",
      "**Secrets**: never read, print, or move credentials, keys, certificates (*.pem, *.key), .env files, ~/.ssh or ~/.aws",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any host, namespace, cluster, database, or container whose name carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources, and anything tagged `prod` or `production`",
      "**Commits and pushes**: never commit or push without the user's explicit authorization for that specific commit/push, in any repository"
    ]
  }
